; =========================================================================
; jdrive.mac - the J-drive, the fuel injectors and the fuel collector,
; as Legend has them (Use_J_Drive in Engine/eObjPilot.a80).
;
; One key, HELD (KB_JDRIVE).  While nothing mass-locks the drive it is
; the J-drive: everything but the bodies and the bays leaves the sky
; (ClearAroundObj), and every body and bay comes JD_STEP nearer a frame
; along z and on past you (proc_07: only z moves), which is how a world
; three minutes off is reached in ten seconds.  What locks it: a bay
; within BASE_U on every axis (Legend's DockingObjNear: all three high
; bytes zero), a ship on the scanner (its oFlg_4 bit 3 clear - drops
; do not lock it, rocks do), and - this port's own, because its worlds
; are bigger than Legend's #4000 - a world or a sun within JD_BODY.
;
; Locked, the same key is the injectors, if a pair is fitted and whole
; and there is fuel: the throttle is overridden with INJ_SPEED, or the
; military pair's INJ_SPEED_MIL, the stick is dead (BlockControl = 2),
; and a tenth of fuel goes every INJ_FRAMES.  Coming straight off the
; drive onto the injectors is refused for a frame (var_12), as Legend
; refuses it.  The fuel collector, fitted and whole, makes a tenth every
; COLL_FRAMES of drive.
; =========================================================================
JD_SPEED:	.WORD	0		; the injectors' speed; 0 = the throttle's
JD_LAST:	.WORD	0		; the key last frame: 0 nothing, 1 the
				;   drive, 2 the injectors (var_12)
JD_FUELT:	.WORD	INJ_FRAMES	; var_07
JD_COLLT:	.WORD	COLL_FRAMES	; var_08
JD_LOCKED:	.WORD	0		; 1 while the key is held on a locked
				;   drive, for the verifier
JD_I:		.WORD	0
